# One sequential, offline catalog journey. No tool or provider execution.
name: Capability selection, prerequisites and draft ownership
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait-for: 25 Start Map
submit: modules
wait-for: 15 CAPABILITIES
live-snap: map-actions
expect: Quick map
expect: Deep threat map
ask: Does the catalog distinguish planning from execution, with prerequisites disclosed rather than registration presented as readiness?
keys: Down
wait-live-snap: 10 MODEL REQUIRED | selected-threat-map
expect: MODEL REQUIRED
ask: Does the next-action hint describe the selected threat-map row, including any unresolved model or input requirement?
keys: Enter
wait-live-snap: 10 no work started | loaded-draft
expect: run threat-model:build
expect-not: RUN FOCUS
expect: no work started
ask: Does Enter load an editable command without launching work, and is that distinction visible?
keys: C-u
wait-for: 15 CAPABILITIES
resize: 160x48
live-snap: catalog-160x48
expect: MODEL REQUIRED
ask: At 160x48, does the selected action retain its prerequisite and draft-loading guidance without conflicting readiness claims?
resize: 96x89
live-snap: catalog-96x89
expect: MODEL REQUIRED
ask: At 96x89, is selection still attached to the same action, with input ownership and loading controls visible?
resize: 80x24
live-snap: catalog-80x24
ask: Can the operator read the selected action and its prerequisites at 80x24 and identify the load control?
resize: 60x20
live-snap: catalog-60x20
expect: MODEL REQUIRED
ask: At 60x20, can the operator see the selected action and its preparation requirement without losing the cursor or draft?
resize: 40x12
live-snap: catalog-40x12
expect: MODEL REQUIRED
ask: At 40x12, are the selected action and its next step readable rather than hidden behind the catalog header?
keys: C-c
wait-for: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT
keys: y
require-exit: 10
resize: 120x36
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait-for: 25 Start Map
submit: modules
wait-for: 15 CAPABILITIES
keys: Down
live-snap: catalog-no-color
expect: MODEL REQUIRED
ask: Are readiness and selection understandable without color, with no work started?
keys: C-c
wait-for: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT
keys: y
require-exit: 10
